      "id": 9346,
      "name": "SuperRick",
      "username": "SuperRick",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/superrick/{size}/2705_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-01-31T20:44:23.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Okay guys, I'm looking for some simple house-rule&nbsp;ideas to common questions.&nbsp; Let me reinforce the idea: <strong><em>simple ideas.&nbsp; </em></strong>Here are some ideas&nbsp;I think work but I'd love to hear other ideas:</p><p><strong>1. Making Ambuscade Better:</strong>&nbsp; Double his HP&nbsp;and the amount of cards he plays every turn.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>2. Two Hero Variant game:</strong>&nbsp; Increase both heroes HP by 15, each turn one hero gets&nbsp;an extra power and the other draws an extra card, the following turn they switch.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong>3. Playing against multiple villians (other than V5):</strong>&nbsp; Very tough because of the diversity amongst the villians.&nbsp; I know HP isn't everything, but my best guess is to divide the individual villian's HP by the total&nbsp;number of villians.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>For the designers who may happen to read this thread, I want to say this isn't meant to be critical as SotM is by far my favorite game.&nbsp; That's why I called the thread \"simple ideas\" not \"simple solutions.\"&nbsp; I don't think the game has problems, but sometimes people may want to just play it a little differently!</p><p>Anyone else have some ideas?&nbsp; Anyone willing to try these (or some other ideas that may be posted) and share thier experience?&nbsp; I've already tried the two-hero variant and its worked great.&nbsp; I'd really like to hear some other ideas.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:40:07.005Z",
