      "raw": "<p>Okay guys, I&#39;m looking for some simple house-rule&nbsp;ideas to common questions.&nbsp; Let me reinforce the idea: <strong><em>simple ideas.&nbsp; </em></strong>Here are some ideas&nbsp;I think work but I&#39;d love to hear other ideas:</p><p><strong>1. Making Ambuscade Better:</strong>&nbsp; Double his HP&nbsp;and the amount of cards he plays every turn.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>2. Two Hero Variant game:</strong>&nbsp; Increase both heroes HP by 15, each turn one hero gets&nbsp;an extra power and the other draws an extra card, the following turn they switch.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p><strong>3. Playing against multiple villians (other than V5):</strong>&nbsp; Very tough because of the diversity amongst the villians.&nbsp; I know HP isn&#39;t everything, but my best guess is to divide the individual villian&#39;s HP by the total&nbsp;number of villians.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>For the designers who may happen to read this thread, I want to say this isn&#39;t meant to be critical as SotM is by far my favorite game.&nbsp; That&#39;s why I called the thread &quot;simple ideas&quot; not &quot;simple solutions.&quot;&nbsp; I don&#39;t think the game has problems, but sometimes people may want to just play it a little differently!</p><p>Anyone else have some ideas?&nbsp; Anyone willing to try these (or some other ideas that may be posted) and share thier experience?&nbsp; I&#39;ve already tried the two-hero variant and its worked great.&nbsp; I&#39;d really like to hear some other ideas.</p><p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>",
